[evidence."cameras.main.keep_in_view_rows"]
source = "observed"
confidence = 85
note = "Touching Kong on 25m: Mario never reaches him. The edge test $D990 that the walk ($D1F3) and the jump call also refuses a move left on 25m ($53 = 1) while the girder byte $59 is 6, Kong's girder, and Mario's sprite x is 104 or less ($D9C3-$D9DB; on 75m the same on girder 5). $59 is the girder from the sprite's y by the thresholds at $C0BC ($E016: sprite y 40 to 67 is girder 6, so y 45 to 72), set by the walk and the climb's end, and kept through a jump, so the jump's turn takes the takeoff height. No death test names Kong ($EC44 barrels, $ED8A fires, $EDC5 the oil drum). Probe kong-wall (clear-25m clip 2): Left held from x 179 on girder 6 stops at x 109 at frame 2986, where a barrel hits him at 3003"

[[evidence."cameras.main.keep_in_view_rows".refs]]
at = "clip:donkey-kong-ju-clear-25m-002"

[evidence."cameras.main.keep_in_view_turn"]
source = "observed"
confidence = 85
note = "The jump routine ($D547) calls $D990 before it moves Mario: with his way right ($56 = 1) and his sprite x at 224 or more (x 229), or left and 16 or less (x 21), it flips $56 and $57, so he comes back the other way. The walk routine ($D1E5) calls the same test and doesn't move him (keep_in_view). Worker D's probe of a jump into the right edge turned him around in the air"

