note = """The screen is the NES's (256 by 240, 8/7 pixels, 8 lines hidden top and bottom) with its 8 sprites a line; the game keeps every object in a fixed part of the sprite table ($0200 Mario, $0230 + 16k barrels, $02C0 points, $02D0 hammers, $02E0 the fire and Pauline), so it never turns their order and nothing flickers (sprite table of every frame of recordings dk-clear-25m, dk-death-path and dk-hammer-001). The status box is the string screen_25m_more; the status routine writes the score 6 digits from row 3 column 4, the top score from column 16, the lives at row 5 column 21, the bonus 4 digits from column 23 and the level at column 28, all in background palette 3 (attribute bytes $FF and $0F). screen_25m_more writes a second player's label ($FE $FF) at row 3 column 22, which the stage setup blanks; a field of two blanks ($24) stands for that. Presentation: Presentation (docs/model.md, "Presentation"). The game draws with $F096: a grid of sprites from a first tile, a column at a time, so a 2 by 2 frame from tile T is T and T+1 down its left column and T+2 and T+3 down its right, written here row by row. Mode 1 ($F086) mirrors the grid, the whole picture flipped. Sprite palette n is the set's palette 4 + n. Sound: The game's sound requests as sound roles (core present.sound_roles), so a theme can replace each with a file. The driver (dk_sound) takes $FF (pulse 1 effects), $FE (pulse 2), $FD (music) by bit the frame after a routine sets them and clears them; $FC holds the tune the game keeps set. The bits are the driver's: $FBF2 takes $FF's lowest bit first, $FD67 starts song n for $FD's bit n. `gp theme kit` lists them with the lengths it measures from the model's own sound (docs/theme-kit.md). The attract demo sets the stage's tune request ($FC = $02) with the sound channels off ($4015, $CE85), so the game is silent while it plays. Cells: A taken rivet's or prize's tiles (platformer level.pickup_cells) are drawn as the blank tile $24, which $EF38 writes there. Screens: The title screen (core present.screens): the string the title routine draws ($C807 with 8, $C914-$C91E) and its cursor, sprite 0 with tile $A2 at x 56 and y $0511 ($C921-$C935), 16 lines down a menu line. The stage setup after a death or a clear turns the picture off: the screen is the backdrop from the divider wrap that takes the wait ($43, death_wait or clear_wait) to 19 until the third frame after the wrap that takes it to 15, when the new stage is drawn (hammer clip 5, frames 304 to 350; game B clip 1, 373 to 419; clear-25m clip 1 from 1826). A picture shows the state the frame before it, so the screens hold from the last frame of 20 to the second of 15. Screens: Start on the title begins the death's wait from $43 = 151 with the title left on the screen ($C98A draws nothing) until the stage setup blanks it: start_title, which Start on the title sets (title clip 2, frames 57 to 372). Start in the demo leaves the demo's stage on the screen instead (title clip 10 from 1147)."""

